 ('hbrownbaisri', ('hbrownbaisri',), 'max', '2:3', "a Thai 'bai sri' offering of dried brown banana leaf, about 45 centimetres tall, standing in a shiny gold embossed pedestal bowl on a waisted foot: five or six thick upright clusters of dark chocolate-brown plaited leaf fingers, each cluster curving outward like the hood of a many-headed naga, every finger tipped with a small white bead bud; in the middle a taller slim spire of the same wrapped brown leaf ending in a small stacked knob finial, with a tiny pink ribbon bow tied to it. No flowers, no blossoms and no hanging drops anywhere on it: only the brown leaf, the white bead buds, the one tiny pink bow and the gold bowl."),
 ('hgreencol', ('hgreencol',), 'max', '9:16', "a tall slim Thai temple altar ornament about 2.6 metres tall and 30 centimetres across: a straight dark-green pole carrying SEVEN tiers one above another, evenly spaced; each tier is a small shallow round dish of dull olive-gold with a ring of dull yellow-gold cloth roses round its rim, and standing in the dish round the pole four or five glossy dark-green satin leaves, some curling outward at the tip like the crested heads of little nagas and some spiky like fern fronds, each edged with tiny white pearl dots; a closed creamy-white lotus bud on the very top; the pole stands on a small plain round dark-green foot. The whole column from the bud to the ground is inside the frame, perfectly vertical."),
 ('hconetower', ('hconetower', 'hconetower5'), 'max', '2:3', "a Thai altar offering tower about 1.45 metres tall and only about 28 centimetres across at its foot, of the Isan kind called khan mak beng: a TALL SLIM cone, five times as tall as it is wide, built of SEVEN tiers of spiky dark-green folded-leaf fronds pointing upward, each tier resting on a narrow gold band, with small red and pink artificial flowers set round each band and dark maroon folded-leaf buds and a few small white points standing inside each tier, a three-pointed leaf crest at the very top, standing on a small round gold base. The references show only the UPPER FIVE tiers of the real tower, small and soft, cut off at the bottom by things standing before it: the whole tower has seven tiers and tapers evenly from its foot to its tip."),
 ('hlotusvase', ('hlotusvase', 'hlotusvase2'), 'max', '2:3', "a bouquet of artificial white lotus flowers in a vase, about 55 centimetres tall overall: a ceramic vase with a narrow neck and a swelling shoulder, cream coloured, carved all over with large raised spiral scrolls picked out in warm tan-brown, with a plain pale band at its foot; and in it ONE compact rounded dome of about nine LARGE open white cloth lotus flowers with many pointed petals, each bloom big, about a third of the dome's width, packed tightly side by side so the dome is one solid closed mass with no gaps between them; three closed pale green-yellow lotus buds standing just above the dome on short thick stems; and a few broad green leaves round the foot of the dome where it meets the vase. No small flowers, no sprigs, no berries, no thin stems and no sprays sticking out. Simple bold shapes with a clean silhouette."),
 ('hwheel', ('hwheel', 'hwheel4', 'wwheel'), 'max', '2:3', "a Thai ritual offering sculpture about 1.1 metres tall made of dried dark-brown leaf, of the kind called a bai sri Dhamma wheel. At the top an upright WHEEL about 77 centimetres across: a thick ring of wrapped dark-brown leaf bristling all round its outside with short pointed leaf spikes, with EIGHT thick wrapped-leaf spokes and a round hub, open between the spokes, with nothing tucked between them. A NAGA serpent is coiled round the left side of the wheel: its body is covered in small pointed scales of cream-white and dark brown like a pine cone and loops down round the wheel's lower left; its head rears beside the rim at the wheel's upper left, with a red open mouth, a little gold at its jaws and a tall mane of long pointed silver-white leaf spikes swept back from its head. Lying along the top of the rim is a second, small dark-brown naga with a branching horn-like crest. From the very top of the wheel rises a small gilded spray of five golden lotus buds on a thin gold stem. The wheel stands on a drum-shaped base of FOUR thick stacked rings of smooth wrapped brown leaf, each ring studded round its side with a row of small white pointed leaf tips, the lowest ring a little wider; and the base sits on a low round dark rattan stand with an openwork foot. THE REFERENCES: the first two are ragged cut-outs of the real sculpture (where the inside of its wheel is a flat brown patch, the photograph was painted over: draw the eight spokes and the hub there). The third is ANOTHER piece of the same kind, in gold and silver: use it only to understand how such a wheel, its naga and its finial are built, NOT for its colours, its flowers or its base."),
