# the hall's inside: what follows a prompt that has crops (HALLNOTE); and, where one of its references is a WEB
# photograph of the kind of thing (a crop named w...: crops_hallin.py), WEBNOTE instead: its own words then say which
# reference is the real piece and which only shows how such a thing is made, and HALLNOTE's "match exactly" would
# contradict them
WEBNOTE = (" Draw the WHOLE object, complete and undamaged, with every part a cut-out leaves out or cuts off, and ignore "
           "the cut-outs' white gaps and edges and everything in a reference's background.")
HALLNOTE = (" Match the object in the reference photograph(s) exactly: its shapes, materials, colours and proportions. Each "
            "reference is a ragged cut-out of the real object from a photograph: draw the WHOLE object, complete and "
            "undamaged, with every part the cut-out leaves out or cuts off, and ignore the cut-out's white gaps and edges.")
